---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import "../../styles/docs.css";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const shot = `${base}images/guides/reconcile.png`;
---

<Base
	title="Modern Reconcile | Actual Budget Tweaks"
	description="Match an account to your statement from a side panel in Actual Budget Tweaks."
>
	<main class="docs center">
		<header class="docs__header stack stack--sm">
			<a href="/guides" class="docs__back">Back to guides</a>
			<h1>Modern Reconcile</h1>
			<p class="docs__lead">
				Modern Reconcile replaces Actual's reconcile popover and banner with a side panel. The panel
				shows live balances and lists the transactions you haven't cleared.
			</p>
		</header>

		<section class="docs__section">
			<h2>Starting a reconcile</h2>
			<p>Turn on Modern Reconcile in the Accounts &amp; Transactions section of Tweaks, then:</p>
			<ol>
				<li>
					Open the account and click <strong>Reconcile</strong> in its toolbar. The label beside it
					shows how long it's been since the last reconcile. You can also press
					<code>Cmd+K</code> or <code>Ctrl+K</code>, choose <strong>Reconcile account</strong> and
					pick the account.
				</li>
				<li>
					Enter the ending balance from your statement or your bank's app. The box starts with your
					cleared balance. Accounts with bank sync also offer
					<strong>Use bank's synced balance</strong>.
				</li>
				<li>Click <strong>Start reconciling</strong>.</li>
			</ol>
			<p>The sidebar collapses to give the transaction table more room, and comes back when you finish.</p>
		</section>

		<section class="docs__section">
			<h2>Using the panel</h2>
			<a href={shot} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
				<img
					class="docs__shot"
					src={shot}
					width="1400"
					height="860"
					alt="An account being reconciled, with numbered callouts on the toolbar button and on the side panel's amount left to match, list of uncleared transactions, adjustment button and finish button"
				/>
			</a>
			<ol>
				<li>The toolbar button reads <strong>Reconciling...</strong> until you finish.</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Left to match</strong> is your statement balance minus your cleared balance. The
					ring shows how many of the transactions are cleared.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Not cleared</strong> lists your newest uncleared transactions. Click a check mark
					to clear one. Ticking a transaction in the table updates the panel too.
				</li>
				<li>
					If you can't find the difference, the adjustment button adds a cleared transaction for the
					exact amount. It runs through your rules and has the note "Reconciliation balance
					adjustment".
				</li>
				<li><strong>Finish reconciling</strong> is available once the difference is zero.</li>
			</ol>
		</section>

		<section class="docs__section">
			<h2>Finishing</h2>
			<p>
				Finishing locks every cleared transaction in the account and records the reconcile date. A
				notification offers <strong>Undo</strong> for 12 seconds. Reconcile Confetti, on by default,
				adds a burst of confetti.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="docs__section">
			<h2>Stopping early</h2>
			<p>
				<strong>Back</strong> returns to the statement balance so you can change it.
				<strong>Cancel</strong> ends the reconcile without locking anything, and so does closing the
				panel or leaving the account. Transactions you cleared stay cleared, and any adjustment stays
				in the account.
			</p>
		</section>
	</main>
</Base>
